he low of <strong>25\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Dubuque's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Dubuque has set <strong>70 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 64 that chance alone would give, and <strong>52 record highs</strong>, close to the 64 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (76). Dubuque's all-time high is 110\u00b0F, on July 14, 1936.","t_chg":"Dubuque's nights cooled over the long run. Its days show no clear change.","p_chg":"Across 151 complete years: Dubuque's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.09\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.16 to \u22120.02), about \u22121.4\u00b0F since 1875. Dubuque's average high shows no clear change: \u22120.06\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.12 to +0.01) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. July and August highs have edged down across the full record; the 1930s summers were the hottest in it.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 7 months fell. Highs rose in none; July and August fell.","t_rain":"Dubuque has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Dubuque's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.36 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.07 to +0.65), about +5.4 inches since 1874. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 38.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1961 (63.39 in); the driest, 1894 (19.35 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}